{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_018AuST1TRpmBsaLrScqXAXk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q10: Design a safe and debuggable agent loop** (`03-010-design-a-safe-and-debuggable-agent-loop.md`):\n\n**Five-layer framework:**\n1. **Hard limits in orchestrator code** — `max_iterations`, wall-clock timeout, per-step token cap, cumulative session budget (all in Python, never in the prompt)\n2. **Structured trace logging** — every iteration emits JSON with `run_id`, step number, thought, action, observation, token count; threaded run_id enables full replay in LangSmith/OpenTelemetry\n3. **HITL gates before irreversible actions** — classify tools as read vs write; write tools (send_email, charge_card) trigger `interrupt_before` in LangGraph, pausing the graph until human approval\n4. **Idempotent tool execution with retries** — 5s timeout + single retry; failures return a structured error to the LLM so it can self-correct before escalating\n5. **Checkpointed state** — every step written to Redis/Postgres for resumability, replay, and ops inspection (LangGraph's `PostgresSaver` does this natively)\n\n**Key pitfalls covered:** putting safety gates in the prompt (can be jailbroken), no run ID making traces unreplayable, and non-idempotent tools without retry handling.\n\n**29 items remain** in the Next queue."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":275,"cache_read_input_tokens":65434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":275,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8089e9af-882e-43de-ab55-2352579729ca","uuid":"c4a55e9d-c372-4f8f-ab96-c2b52125f89a"}
